# Git workflow

Simplified Git Flow:

```
main          ← stable, deployable, PROTECTED (PRs only, no force-push)
  ↑ merge when a milestone is finished and tested
develop       ← integration branch, source of truth for new features
  ↑ Pull Request
feature/<short-name>
```

## Branches

- New work starts from `develop`:
  ```bash
  git checkout develop && git pull
  git checkout -b feature/<name>
  ```
- Naming: `feature/auth-supabase`, `fix/login-redirect-loop`, `chore/upgrade-deps`
- PRs target `develop`. Squash recommended when merging.
- `develop` → `main` only when a set of features is stable and tested.

## Commits — Conventional Commits

```
feat:     new feature
fix:      bug fix
chore:    maintenance (deps, configs)
refactor: refactor without behavior change
docs:     documentation
test:     tests
style:    formatting
```

Example: `feat(auth): add sign-in form with email/password validation`

## Language

- ALL repository content in **English**: README, code comments, commit messages, branch names, PR titles/descriptions, issues, error messages, log strings.
- Chat conversations with the user remain in **Brazilian Portuguese**.
- Reason: project doubles as international portfolio and forces practice of the technical English vocabulary that the app itself teaches.
